{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/120248-sidereal-charms-do-not-work-that-way-and-other-forum-memes","id":120248,"title":"Sidereal Charms Do Not Work That Way! (And other forum memes)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Sidereal Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-04-27T02:15:05-07:00","id":120248,"title":"Sidereal Charms Do Not Work That Way! (And other forum memes)","content":"Okay, so, I'm a little tired of certain memes getting brought up by the fandom, so I decided I'd make a thread where we separate what exists in the books from what exists in our own twisted psyches. The one I'd like to address right now is one that has resurfaced thanks to the new Ex3 comic*: Sidereal Charms are meant to work only in weird or indirect ways, and Sidereals work best when they plan.<br /> <br /> <b>Sidereal Charms Work Indirectly</b><b>/Weirdly</b><br /> <br /> No they don't- at least, not nearly to the degree that fans say they do. For the most part, Charms from previous editions have functioned exactly how they appear to function, and their uses are immediately obvious and applicable to whichever ability they fall under. Sidereal Melee Charms make you better at hitting people; Sidereal Dodge Charm help you evade harm; Sidereal Socialize Charms help you to manipulate people's Intimacies.<br /> <br /> The only difference between Sidereal Charms and other Exalted Charms is, usually, limitation in scope: Athletics Charms are mostly focused on turning you into the Juggernaut (bitch), Resistance Charms are most effective in turning you into a tank in combat (and less with resisting non-combat hazards like extreme temperatures or weather), and Occult Charms are most effective when dealing with gods and elementals (less so with raksha and demons). There are also some Charms that have effects outside their associated ability (like Defense of Shining Joy from Performance), but they share that property with many Dragon-Blooded Charms (such as the Performance Charms that aid with Stealth, and Lore Charms that are combat-focused).<br /> <br /> This remains true even of Sidereal Martial Arts. The disease effects of Citrine Poxes of Contagion are not all that different from the effects of Cold-Fire Desolation Brand and its upgrades, with similar combat applicability; the Scarlet Patterned Battlefield is simply a mass combat-focused MA; Charcoal March of Spiders is not that distinct from other flurry- and speed-heavy combat styles, with the distinction of the ever notable Pattern Spider Touch; and so on.<br /> <br /> My point is this: let's not pretend that Sidereal Charms are as weird as we like to think they are. Not only is it a false representation of how actual Sidereal Charms work, but it scares away potential readers who might be terrified by claims of oddity that, frankly, don't have much merit.<br /> <br /> <b>Sidereals Work Best When They Plan Ahead</b><br /> <br /> I think this claim is based on the (largely theoretical) powers of Sidereal Astrology: namely, the ability to predict the future by reading the Loom of Fate, the ability to shape the future with Astrology, and the ability to prepare beforehand by &quot;equipping&quot; appropriate Resplendent Destinies. Of course, this has run into two problems: 1) the predictive ability of any divination power is always largely a matter of ST Fiat, and the mechanics for predictions through Astrology (or the various Lore and Investigation Charms related to fortune telling) are vague at best; and 2) the system for creating Destinies has been borked for quite some time, generally ranging from utterly broken to utterly useless with little in-beetween.<br /> <br /> The result is that, in practice, Sidereals wind up no more prepared than anyone else, since a) their predictive abilities are determined entirely by the ST's willingness to provide useful information and b) the only real &quot;preparations&quot; they could reasonably make are indistinguishable from the scene-long or indefinite Charm commitments that literally every other Essence user in the game has to make. If their mechanics were less broken, this meme <i>might</i> have some merit to it, but as it stands, Sidereals wind up just as surprised as anyone else would be of their relative power levels.<br /> <br /> * Which I quite enjoyed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;We do not quit playing because we grow old, we grow old because we quit playing.&quot; - Oliver Wendell Holmes","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/283-mrinsecure","name":"MrInsecure","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar283_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"385"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-27T04:15:16-07:00","id":120274,"title":"","content":"There tends to be a way certain storytellers run Sidereal NPCs that reinforce a lot of misconceptions about them.<br /> I know at least one person who sincerely believes that virtually every Sidereal their PCs encounter will Avoidance Kata away without provocation, pride secrecy above all else and generally add nothing to the game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>success is the ability to go from one failure to the next without any loss of enthusiasm","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1115-the-hug-ninja","name":"The Hug Ninja","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1115_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"324"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-27T04:48:19-07:00","id":120290,"title":"","content":"I just wondering, but do all those people screaming &quot;Sid build house using potato plus ducktape!&quot; and &quot;Sid is ninja!&quot; ever actually play one or they're just talking about the &quot;perfected&quot; Sidereal that is in their head.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":298,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","user":"Jen","date":". 04-27-2014, 07:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-27T07:22:50-07:00","id":120319,"title":"","content":"I agree that Sidereal charms aren't quite as strange as internet exaggeration likes to present, but lets not kid ourselves here:<br /> <br /> - If your friend has a gash in their stomach after the last combat, the best ways to heal are via archery and (depending on the source) craft. Medicine can heal, but only defers the wounds to later in the future.<br /> <br /> - If you want to be able to socially deceive people, your go-to charm is currently in Larceny, and ability that isn't generally used for social combat.<br /> <br /> - There is a ride charm which do not require you to be riding anything to function, and has no altered effect if you are riding something.<br /> <br /> - There are charms which function purely as selective social attacks under resistance and survival.<br /> <br /> - There is no awareness charm that gives you a better chance of spotting an enemy hiding in the bushes, aside from letting you know that there might be something to look for nearby.<br /> <br /> <br /> Let's not hide this fact from them. If a new player is scared away from playing a Sidereal based on the fact that they sound weird, they will probably play something like a Solar that sounds less weird. If a new player decides to play a Sidereal doctor with a high medicine score because they want to be a healer, or takes a high larceny score because they want to play a thief, they're likely to come away with a bad impression of Exalted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":894,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/894-skeptic-tank","user":"Skeptic Tank","date":". 04-27-2014, 10:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/894-skeptic-tank","name":"Skeptic Tank","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar894_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-27T09:08:24-07:00","id":120372,"title":"","content":"Having played a Sidereal for a while and written a bunch of custom Charms, this is what I have to say:<br /> <br /> Sideways Charm use is a thing, though it's been blown way out of proportion. This is probably because of the whole &quot;no custom Charms!&quot; thing and that Sidereals for most of their existence in the game have had a more limited toolbox to draw from, encouraging more creative use. Their Charms do what they say they do, and most are very straightforward.<br /> <br /> Weirdness comes in odd Charm placement in Abilities, though Dragon-Blooded have this too so it's not unique to Sidereals. Still, it's usually worse for Sidereals than DBs, as Sidereals have trees that have extremely few functions directly related to the Ability at hand (Ride, Bureaucracy, Craft), which DBs don't have if I recall correctly. Plus I think there's an expectation for what a Celestial should be able to do which is not there for Terrestrials. So the DBs have an excuse for certain capabilities being absent: they're Terrestrial, they're supposed to be weaker.<br /> <br /> I'd say in reply to Skeptic Tank that you're only partially right. While there are oddball Charm placement, rarely do you go wrong just picking whatever Ability makes the most sense for the character. You may not end up with the same range of competencies as if you were playing a Solar, and you might be able to do things you wouldn't think you'd be able to, but you won't be bad at the stuff you picked. A player wanting to play a healer will do just fine taking Medicine, and they'll happen to be able to fuck up undead too. A player wanting to be a thief will do just fine taking Larceny, and will happen to be able to do some social stuff and mess with people's dice pools on the side. That's what's so fun about playing Sidereals, to me --- by virtue of the Abilities you decide on, you'll be able to pick up some capabilities that a more straightforward splat like Solars wouldn't get. My no-combat-Abilities Serenity has one of the best Dodge DVs of the group due to Defense of Shining Joy, and that's awesome. Anyway:<br /> <br /> -Friend gets cut up? Medicine will ease the wounds, remove any infection, and instantly temporarily remove the wound itself. Yeah, if you're extremely good at Archery, or the source of the attack is outside of Creation or sorcery, then Archery/Craft can do better. Medicine is still a great investment for someone who wants to do medical stuff.<br /> <br /> -Avoiding the Truth is great at deceiving people in the particular way of getting them to believe the opposite of what you said, which is often best used when not trying to deceive but just get people to believe something. To be actually good at pure deception the Fateful Socialize Excellency is probably your best bet. To be generally good at social stuff, the majority of it is in Linguistics, Performance, Presence, and Socialize. Avoiding the Truth, Icy Hand, and Many Missiles Arrow are basically the only oddball social Charms outside the scattering of spirit-related Charms that are across the entire Charmset.<br /> <br /> -While a lot of Ride Charms are not related to Ride, they can definitely improve a mount (or not, of course; Ride is one of the weirder sets). Yellow Path, while it doesn't require riding, it very well may, and is related to travel, which Ride is generally about. Ride is one of the weirder ones, I'll happily admit.<br /> <br /> -Social spirit Charms are in Resistance, Survival, Sail, Occult. Spirit effects are one of those motifs that Sidereals have, so you get social spirit Charms scattered everywhere. There are other social Charms in Drive and Stealth, but that's not too weird -- Solars have a social Charm in Stealth, War, Ride, and Sail.<br /> <br /> -Prior Warning gives you a bonus success for noticing the danger that it told you about, which definitely would be an enemy in the bushes. Expected Pain negates whatever stealth they had when they attack. Supernal Vision lets you <i>know</i> the enemy is there, if you happen to be looking for &quot;people hiding&quot;. Sidereal Awareness is very good at finding things, even if it doesn't have any ways to directly enhance senses.<br /> <br /> Alright, that said, let's take a look at Dragon-Blooded:<br /> <br /> -Combat defend-other charm in Linguistics.<br /> -Attack Charms in Lore.<br /> -What is really a Sail or archery-defense Charm in Occult.<br /> -Sensory-boosting and movement-enhancement in Stealth.<br /> -Soak defense in Thrown.<br /> -Put people to sleep, screw with their motes, or literally kill people with Awareness.<br /> -A movement effect in Craft.<br /> -Strength enhancement in Resistance.<br /> -Damage booster in Athletics (though Solars have one too).<br /> -Boost soak and health, or make attacks, with Presence.<br /> -Instantly form mass combat units with Socialize.<br /> -Temporarily seize control of a chosen vessel's mind and body when you die with Bureaucracy.<br /> -Lots of sensory effects in Larceny. Really if you want sense-boosting there's more in Larceny than Awareness.<br /> -Sickness attack Charm in Medicine (not too far off base, but still an attack booster), along with changing your anima or protecting yourself against disease or toxin (which would normally be Resistance.)<br /> -Stealth and combat Charms in Performance.<br /> -Medicine effects in Survival.<br /> <br /> Wow that's a lot of weird placement. Might even be more than Sidereals have.<br /> <br /> Now that I think about it, I feel that the reason DBs are not felt to be as weird as Sidereals is because it's easier to see and understand elemental associations than it is the thematic associations that define the Sidereal Charmset. Strip away the thematic reasoning, and it looks to me like Dragon-Blooded have more oddball Charm placements than Sidereals by far.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/11I0xCPgAS3ZhxGvTlBoePOuaDqgpyWs13jVKhJ4c8hM/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Book of the Emerald Circle</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/37100-white-elephant-for-flintlock-sidereal-custom-charms-and-discussion-on-themes\" target=\"_blank\">Custom Sidereal Charms</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sQxyi3ox0qn53c_vsUaVQi_pRdpKlQE50NT5ldQmxYI/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Expanded Sidereal Linguistics</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/263-limited-reagent","name":"Limited Reagent","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar263_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"591"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-27T09:12:15-07:00","id":120374,"title":"","content":"<br /> Some of their Charms do reward careful thinking about how exactly they can be used, like Easily Accepted Proposition Stance and Avoiding the Truth Technique, some don't as much. <br /> <br /> The idea that they're the Google interview question style &quot;You're butt naked with a rubber chicken. How do you save the world?&quot; Exalted seems a bit overcooked.<br /> <br /> It seems to me their magic is of the form where each Ability has a fairly clear theme, and where each their Charms generally have clear uses that almost never contradict the Ability but also have other &quot;Eureka!&quot; uses if you think about them more carefully. Not really &quot;What the heck are all these random Charms that are tenuously connected to this Ability?&quot;. (When I say contradict, I mean that Sidereal Charms are almost never of the sort where the Charm actually pushes the character away from the concept of &quot;Ability X&quot; master, but they often do not specifically enhance that character at that Ability.)<br /> <br /> I get the impression that Sidereal Charms are meant to make the average player feel like they're thinking like a Sidereal, heroes who face limitations in their powers and work with restrictions (like Fate) and overcome them through cleverness, efficiency, brilliant insights and deftness, but they're not like the Advanced Super Puzzle Exalted. Is that like the play experience?<br /> <br /> Sidereals working best when they plan ahead is supposed to come through via their Charms requiring some forethought and planning to use to their maximum strength, which is a much more elegant way of doing it than putting in a &quot;plans&quot; mechanic.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Skeptic Tank</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/120248-sidereal-charms-do-not-work-that-way-and-other-forum-memes?p=120319#post120319\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let's not hide this fact from them. If a new player is scared away from playing a Sidereal based on the fact that they sound weird, they will probably play something like a Solar that sounds less weird. If a new player decides to play a Sidereal doctor with a high medicine score because they want to be a healer, or takes a high larceny score because they want to play a thief, they're likely to come away with a bad impression of Exalted.</div> </div> </div> </div>If they took the right dots, I expect they'd be quite happy being their thief who was almost without peer among mortals, and had interesting useful magical forms of stealing (that helped them steal secrets, and in the right circumstances and with cleverness made them a better thief than mortals and had other benefits besides). And that would be better than scaring them off with stories about how they'd get all this weird magic that would be useless unless they were really, really sharp.<br /> <br /> But perhaps not so much if they expected to be a supernaturally *talented* thief.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-27T10:08:20-07:00","id":120399,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Skeptic Tank</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/120248-sidereal-charms-do-not-work-that-way-and-other-forum-memes?p=120319#post120319\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you want to be able to socially deceive people, your go-to charm is currently in Larceny, and ability that isn't generally used for social combat.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's always Avoiding the Truth Technique:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=LSNTjX_g9a4\" data-code=\"LSNTjX_g9a4\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/LSNTjX_g9a4/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;We do not quit playing because we grow old, we grow old because we quit playing.&quot; - Oliver Wendell Holmes","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/283-mrinsecure","name":"MrInsecure","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar283_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"385"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-27T11:47:45-07:00","id":120433,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrInsecure</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/120248-sidereal-charms-do-not-work-that-way-and-other-forum-memes#post120248\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <b>Sidereals Work Best When They Plan Ahead</b><br /> <br /> I think this claim is based on the (largely theoretical) powers of Sidereal Astrology: namely, the ability to predict the future by reading the Loom of Fate, the ability to shape the future with Astrology, and the ability to prepare beforehand by &quot;equipping&quot; appropriate Resplendent Destinies. Of course, this has run into two problems: 1) the predictive ability of any divination power is always largely a matter of ST Fiat, and the mechanics for predictions through Astrology (or the various Lore and Investigation Charms related to fortune telling) are vague at best; and 2) the system for creating Destinies has been borked for quite some time, generally ranging from utterly broken to utterly useless with little in-beetween.<br /> <br /> The result is that, in practice, Sidereals wind up no more prepared than anyone else, since a) their predictive abilities are determined entirely by the ST's willingness to provide useful information and b) the only real &quot;preparations&quot; they could reasonably make are indistinguishable from the scene-long or indefinite Charm commitments that literally every other Essence user in the game has to make. If their mechanics were less broken, this meme <i>might</i> have some merit to it, but as it stands, Sidereals wind up just as surprised as anyone else would be of their relative power levels.</div> </div> </div> </div>You actually identified the source of this in your second paragraph- in 1e, the explicit goal was that a lot of important Sidereal charms would be scene-long with simple activations, such that an unprepared Sidereal would be much less powerful than one who came in with all the scene-longs up. I'm not entirely sure if that was significantly different from 1e Solar play, but the differences have certainly faded more than a bit with all of the scene-longs everybody else does in 2e. Since there's less of a mechanical difference, people instead tend to talk about it as using Sidereal powers to prepare the eventual combat scene to your advantage; of course, that's something that any other Exalt could do.<br /> <br /> Practically speaking, the chance of any player actually making a Destiny in response to any given short-term situation is nil, yes.<br /> <br /> Also, while the Lore/Investigation prophecy charms are more than a bit vague, the Awareness ones are exceedingly good at allowing you to avoid being ambushed or prepare a counter-ambush. I've never seen ST fiat water those ones down in the way it might Lore/Investigation, either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/789-mercury","name":"Mercury","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar789_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-27T12:08:24-07:00","id":120446,"title":"","content":"It also is a necessity considering their best combat charms come from a system that before being changed drastically required a lot of preparation. Activating prismatic arrangement and getting into battlemode took minute which in combat is a deathsentence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-27T13:49:54-07:00","id":120500,"title":"","content":"As long as we're talking about annoying fan memes about the Sidereal Charmset...<br /> <br /> The Sidereal Charmset is not actually closed. The Maidens can add to it whenever. But for some bizarre reason fans seem to think it's impossible to make new Charms. It's as if they think the ST can't control the Maidens.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it\" target=\"_blank\">EX3 Craft Rewrite</a><br /> <br /> Sanctaphrax is not a person<br /> -Chejop Kejak","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1154-sanctaphrax","name":"Sanctaphrax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1154_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-27T13:58:52-07:00","id":120510,"title":"","content":"Objectively? Objectively objective, objectivizing objectively.<br /> <br /> (sagenod)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-27T14:20:43-07:00","id":120527,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sanctaphrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/120248-sidereal-charms-do-not-work-that-way-and-other-forum-memes?p=120500#post120500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As long as we're talking about annoying fan memes about the Sidereal Charmset...<br /> <br /> The Sidereal Charmset is not actually closed. The Maidens can add to it whenever. But for some bizarre reason fans seem to think it's impossible to make new Charms. It's as if they think the ST can't control the Maidens.</div> </div> </div> </div>Opening the charmset except for rare times just ruins how the sidereals are supposed to function.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-27T14:36:46-07:00","id":120542,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/120248-sidereal-charms-do-not-work-that-way-and-other-forum-memes?p=120527#post120527\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Opening the charmset except for rare times just ruins how the sidereals are supposed to function.</div> </div> </div> </div>It would be better to say that it's restricted rather than closed, generally. Like spy gear, you won't get new requisitions often, but you can get new requisitions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-27T15:45:21-07:00","id":120586,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/120248-sidereal-charms-do-not-work-that-way-and-other-forum-memes?p=120542#post120542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It would be better to say that it's restricted rather than closed, generally. Like spy gear, you won't get new requisitions often, but you can get new requisitions.</div> </div> </div> </div>You see, there would be a lot less fan rage if it were presented like Q giving Bond his gear rather than &quot;we have all this awesome stuff and <i>you</i> can't have any!&quot;<br /> <br /> Even if there's no functional difference, presentation matters quite a bit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;We do not quit playing because we grow old, we grow old because we quit playing.&quot; - Oliver Wendell Holmes","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/283-mrinsecure","name":"MrInsecure","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar283_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"385"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-27T15:58:11-07:00","id":120590,"title":"","content":"Oh yes, one more irritating meme I'd like to address:<br /> <br /> <b>Infernals Are Transhuman</b><br /> <br /> This is mostly a case of &quot;You Keep Using That Word,&quot; since it's about the least useful and most off-putting way of describing how Infernals work without using the phrase &quot;mandatory rape.&quot; Yes, Infernals are transformed by their Charms, in ways that other Exalted are not- hell, they Exalt <i>by emerging from a Chrysalis</i>. If the metamorphosis symbolism were any more obvious, Infernals would all come out with butterfly wings and be greeted by Ovid himself.<br /> <br /> The issue is that the word &quot;transhuman&quot; has a lot of real world baggage that comes with it- transhumanism is a real philosophical movement with real adherents and detractors, which has <i>nothing</i> to do with what the Infernals are doing. And unlike the use of &quot;demon&quot; or &quot;god&quot; in the context of Exalted, it's not a deliberate invocation of that real world philosophy, it's just fans being lazy and jumping on a meme because they forget that newbies will have exactly zero context for what they're talking about. So let's just kill this meme dead in the water and figure out a better way to talk about our favorite proto-Primordials, shall we?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;We do not quit playing because we grow old, we grow old because we quit playing.&quot; - Oliver Wendell Holmes","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/283-mrinsecure","name":"MrInsecure","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar283_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"385"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-27T16:02:42-07:00","id":120595,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sanctaphrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/120248-sidereal-charms-do-not-work-that-way-and-other-forum-memes?p=120500#post120500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As long as we're talking about annoying fan memes about the Sidereal Charmset...<br /> <br /> The Sidereal Charmset is not actually closed. The Maidens can add to it whenever. But for some bizarre reason fans seem to think it's impossible to make new Charms. It's as if they think the ST can't control the Maidens.</div> </div> </div> </div>Here's the thing. The book mentions that yes, technically it could happen, that a Sidereal could get some new Charms approved by the Maidens, but <i>also</i> that nobody has managed it in roughly forever despite constant attempts.<br /> <br /> When I'm playing a Sidereal, neither the ST nor I expect me to be able to casually do something that smarter, more capable, more influential, and just plain better at their jobs Sidereals have been trying to do for the last fifteen hundred years with a 0% success rateeasily. Things that nobody has been able to do before are arc seeds, not givens. Except that at some level nobody wants to bog the game down with the &quot;not easy&quot; path, because putting the entire circle through an arc just so I can buy some Charms (that aren't even going to <i>solve</i> a poblem because these are still Sidereal Charms) is boring for other players. So, end result: &quot;I'll get to it later&quot; and then the campaign ends before you ever got around to making new charms. <br /> <br /> In fact, funny thing - if the book simply had read &quot;Sidereals can't make new charms, at all&quot;, especifically stated to be impossible, I'm pretty sure there would be MORE Sidereal custom charms being made. The fact that there's a theoretical escape clause, even if it's a clause that basically makes it completely impracticable for most real games, gets it enforced a lot harder.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1793-drascin","name":"Drascin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1793_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"400"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-27T17:13:35-07:00","id":120621,"title":"","content":"Sidereal planning ahead and the influencing Fate thing works much better if one uses the FATE system (big surprise huh?). Aspects and the compelling thereof work great for blessing, curses, prophecies, and the like. Exalted's attempt to emulate these things are not nearly as good, sad to say. I know people love the whole thing about how going against Fate is like swimming upstream - a feat Solars can achieve with little effort - but as a ST I absolutely loathe that meme or whatever you want to call it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/407-ithle","name":"Ithle","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-27T17:43:38-07:00","id":120632,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Drascin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/120248-sidereal-charms-do-not-work-that-way-and-other-forum-memes?p=120595#post120595\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Here's the thing. The book mentions that yes, technically it could happen, that a Sidereal could get some new Charms approved by the Maidens, but <i>also</i> that nobody has managed it in roughly forever despite constant attempts.<br /> <br /> When I'm playing a Sidereal, neither the ST nor I expect me to be able to casually do something that smarter, more capable, more influential, and just plain better at their jobs Sidereals have been trying to do for the last fifteen hundred years with a 0% success rateeasily.</div> </div> </div> </div>I get why that stops players, though I do dislike the way that people often see anything which hasn't been done before as impossible.<br /> <br /> What I don't get is why it stops STs. They can just say &quot;Mars has seen fit to grant you and your comrades a new Melee Charm&quot;. The return of the Solars and the disappearance of the Empress and the creation of Infernals and Abyssals is a great excuse, but you don't actually need an excuse.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it\" target=\"_blank\">EX3 Craft Rewrite</a><br /> <br /> Sanctaphrax is not a person<br /> -Chejop Kejak","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1154-sanctaphrax","name":"Sanctaphrax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1154_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-27T18:18:48-07:00","id":120647,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sanctaphrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/120248-sidereal-charms-do-not-work-that-way-and-other-forum-memes?p=120632#post120632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I get why that stops players, though I do dislike the way that people often see anything which hasn't been done before as impossible.<br /> <br /> What I don't get is why it stops STs. They can just say &quot;Mars has seen fit to grant you and your comrades a new Melee Charm&quot;. The return of the Solars and the disappearance of the Empress and the creation of Infernals and Abyssals is a great excuse, but you don't actually need an excuse.</div> </div> </div> </div>For the most part, probably to keep in line with the theme. The maidens don't give charms because they don't want to or because you deserve it. They give charms out because you need them. The implication is that they have a complete charmset and while extra bells and whistles are nice, that doesn't mean you'll get it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-27T22:36:06-07:00","id":120764,"title":"","content":"Adding a Charm or five wouldn't affect that theme, though. Unless they were filling specific gaps.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it\" target=\"_blank\">EX3 Craft Rewrite</a><br /> <br /> Sanctaphrax is not a person<br /> -Chejop Kejak","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1154-sanctaphrax","name":"Sanctaphrax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1154_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-28T00:54:43-07:00","id":120819,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sanctaphrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/120248-sidereal-charms-do-not-work-that-way-and-other-forum-memes?p=120632#post120632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I get why that stops players, though I do dislike the way that people often see anything which hasn't been done before as impossible.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a difference between &quot;nobody has done this before&quot; and &quot;people have been trying to do this continuously for centuries and nobody even got close to succeeding&quot;. The first one is a decent call to trying and seeing what happens. The second one is telling you that you're not <i>supposed </i>to succeed unless you make a really good effort. But starting a plot solely so you can have some new Charms that, again, aren't even really going to solve problems because that's not how Sidereal Charms work, is not a thing most people want to interrupt the ongoing game for.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sanctaphrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/120248-sidereal-charms-do-not-work-that-way-and-other-forum-memes?p=120632#post120632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What I don't get is why it stops STs. They can just say &quot;Mars has seen fit to grant you and your comrades a new Melee Charm&quot;. The return of the Solars and the disappearance of the Empress and the creation of Infernals and Abyssals is a great excuse, but you don't actually need an excuse.</div> </div> </div> </div>As said, it's most often a psychological matter. People have less trouble waiving impossibility than &quot;really hard&quot;, because if something is stated to be technically possible but really hard it feels like there's an &quot;out&quot; and if you really want it you <i>could </i>do it.<br /> <br /> You need to actually sit down and think deeply about sidereals in an actual game instead of theorethical Sidereals to realize that in this case, this &quot;really hard&quot; and &quot;impossible for all practical purposes&quot; are the same thing in 90% of cases, and react accordingly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1793-drascin","name":"Drascin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1793_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"400"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-28T01:05:10-07:00","id":120822,"title":"","content":"Not really sure why you decide to quote Manual: Sidereals Suck-Harder Ver., what with amazing gems like this decorating the book from start to finish:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> should the dragon judge the call unnecessary, he may bring the Sidereal up on whatever charges he can think of, the least of which will be wasting his time. Sidereals have died rather than call for Celestial intervention\u2014some situations are so politically sensitive that training a new Sidereal causes less trouble for the Bureau of Destiny than dealing with the Bureau of Heaven\u2019s full scrutiny. </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Bull of the North\u2019s anima resembles a mighty bull, and he\u2019s the greatest warlord of the North; and the god of war of the South so happens to be a god of cattle. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-28T02:59:32-07:00","id":120862,"title":"","content":"Sidereal <i>Charms</i> aren't weird, not individually, but in a collective sense and for the sake of orienting them towards various functional goals, they often incentivize Sidereals acting in a weird manner.<br /> <br /> I would also say that there are some Charms and synergies that reward a bit of context control, sometimes in ways that aren't readily apparent. Like making sure that you have vaguely defined appointments all over the place for the sake of Yellow Road, or using some of those Socialize spirit-controlling Charms to define any random room you own as a personal library and then arrange for information drops by locally recruited spies that you can constantly check in on with Efficient Secretaries.<br /> <br /> Any of those Charms <i>can</i> be, and readily are, used exactly as they're written, but how they're written (interpreted through a lens of assuming that Sidereals are naturally about a bit of pedantic cheating) can let you use a bit of lateral thinking to apply them in non-obvious ways.<br /> <br /> I would also say that &quot;preparation&quot; is not always strictly necessary, but can be useful (off the top of my head, I'd say one would prefer to use Avoidance Kata when one's approach to a situation gives them a bit of foreknowledge about where they'll end up), although I think it's mostly just about prayer strips.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-28T08:22:08-07:00","id":120941,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Drascin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/120248-sidereal-charms-do-not-work-that-way-and-other-forum-memes?p=120595#post120595\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's the thing. The book mentions that yes, technically it could happen, that a Sidereal could get some new Charms approved by the Maidens, but <i>also</i> that nobody has managed it in roughly forever despite constant attempts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is odd seeing as there are Charms that realistically couldn't have existed in the Primordial War or the First Age. Breaking the Wild Mortal, for instance, exists solely as a way to bypass Arcane Fate; the Charm would literally do nothing before the Mask got broken.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1369-mewtarthio","name":"Mewtarthio","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-28T08:41:44-07:00","id":120951,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrInsecure</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/120248-sidereal-charms-do-not-work-that-way-and-other-forum-memes?p=120590#post120590\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh yes, one more irritating meme I'd like to address:<br /> <br /> <b>Infernals Are Transhuman</b><br /> <br /> This is mostly a case of &quot;You Keep Using That Word,&quot; since it's about the least useful and most off-putting way of describing how Infernals work without using the phrase &quot;mandatory rape.&quot; Yes, Infernals are transformed by their Charms, in ways that other Exalted are not- hell, they Exalt <i>by emerging from a Chrysalis</i>. If the metamorphosis symbolism were any more obvious, Infernals would all come out with butterfly wings and be greeted by Ovid himself.<br /> <br /> The issue is that the word &quot;transhuman&quot; has a lot of real world baggage that comes with it- transhumanism is a real philosophical movement with real adherents and detractors, which has <i>nothing</i> to do with what the Infernals are doing. And unlike the use of &quot;demon&quot; or &quot;god&quot; in the context of Exalted, it's not a deliberate invocation of that real world philosophy, it's just fans being lazy and jumping on a meme because they forget that newbies will have exactly zero context for what they're talking about. So let's just kill this meme dead in the water and figure out a better way to talk about our favorite proto-Primordials, shall we?</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree wholeheartedly, especially since Infernals will be different to some degree in the new edition. Infernals weren't transhuman, they were alien.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520732-forged-by-purpose-alchemicals-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Forged By Purpose: The Alchemicals</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1413451-dead-but-not-gone-ghosts\" target=\"_blank\">Dead But Not Gone: Ghosts</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/228291-ghosts-a-revision-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Ghosts: A Revision</a> (2nd Edition)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/316-masters-of-the-industrial-elements-2e-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Masters of the Industrial Elements</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1157362-from-the-crucible-crafting-as-a-struggle-peach\" target=\"_blank\">\u200bFrom The Crucible: Crafting As A Struggle</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/74-kyeudo","name":"Kyeudo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar74_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1723"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-28T09:03:24-07:00","id":120966,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mewtarthio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/120248-sidereal-charms-do-not-work-that-way-and-other-forum-memes?p=120941#post120941\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which is odd seeing as there are Charms that realistically couldn't have existed in the Primordial War or the First Age. Breaking the Wild Mortal, for instance, exists solely as a way to bypass Arcane Fate; the Charm would literally do nothing before the Mask got broken.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also the Medicine Charm for use against the undead, which didn't exist before the Underworld took shape. It's possible the Maidens foresaw (or at least predicted) that the need for them would arise, or indeed that they created them only after the fact.<br /> <br /> Drascin may be on the right track with the psychological reason for why it doesn't much happen. The book could stand to be more welcoming on this regard. Hell, just a sidebar saying something like this:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\">&quot;It is possible a Maiden may suddenly summon a player's Sidereal and demonstrate a new Charm -- perhaps the player has wanted to include that Charm and has received Storyteller approval. The Maiden might then dismiss her Sidereal, without explanation for her actions. In time, it may become clear to the Star-Chosen why this Charm was taught then and there, and why to him in particular. Or the reasons may never be understood, beyond serving as another part of the Maidens' far-reaching plans.&quot;</div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":558,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","user":"Gaius","date":".  Tidied up and indented that paragraph. 05-15-2014, 07:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-28T10:30:03-07:00","id":121017,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/120248-sidereal-charms-do-not-work-that-way-and-other-forum-memes?p=120966#post120966\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also the Medicine Charm for use against the undead, which didn't exist before the Underworld took shape. It's possible the Maidens foresaw (or at least predicted) that the need for them would arise, or indeed that they created them only after the fact.<br /> <br /> Drascin may be on the right track with the psychological reason for why it doesn't much happen. The book could certainly stand to be more welcoming on this regard. Hell, just a sidebar saying something to the effect of, &quot;It is entirely possible a Maiden might suddenly summon a player's Sidereal and demonstrate a new Charm, perhaps a Charm that player has wanted to include in the game with Storyteller approval. The Maiden might then dismiss her Sidereal, without explanation for her actions. It may in time become clear to the Star-Chosen why this Charm was taught then and there, and why to him in particular. Or the reasons may never be completely understood, save that it was another step in the Maidens' far-reaching plans.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>There's also the extremely often overlooked possibility of Player/Storyteller-created charms being retroactively added to that game's canon.<br /> I mean, literally nothing prevents the ST from going &quot;yeah, this custom charm has always been part of the Sidereal charmset, it just means that NPCs have access to it&quot;.<br /> (edit: which, iirc, is the direction John and Holden are going with 3e sidereal charms. It is still a closed charmset, but future books will/might retroactively add to it)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":43,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","user":"Fata-Ku","date":". 04-28-2014, 01:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-28T10:45:40-07:00","id":121035,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/120248-sidereal-charms-do-not-work-that-way-and-other-forum-memes?p=121017#post121017\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's also the extremely often overlooked possibility of Player/Storyteller-created charms being retroactively added to that game's canon.<br /> I mean, literally nothing prevents the ST from going &quot;yeah, this custom charm has always been part of the Sidereal charmset, it just means that NPCs have access to it&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Aye, good point. That's certainly the easiest way to get in such a thing.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> (edit: which, iirc, is the direction John and Holden are going with 3e sidereal charms. It is still a closed charmset, but future books will/might retroactively add to it) </div> </div> </div>I believe that's the case: if the game marches on and they decide Sidereals really should have X and/or get to play with mechanic Y, then a Charm fulfilling that need will appear somewhere and be retroactively assumed to have always been there. I don't think they've made a statement on the in-universe creation of new Sidereal Charms in EX3, though, so that will likely remain in some form.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-28T10:49:02-07:00","id":121036,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/120248-sidereal-charms-do-not-work-that-way-and-other-forum-memes?p=121017#post121017\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's also the extremely often overlooked possibility of Player/Storyteller-created charms being retroactively added to that game's canon.<br /> I mean, literally nothing prevents the ST from going &quot;yeah, this custom charm has always been part of the Sidereal charmset, it just means that NPCs have access to it&quot;.<br /> (edit: which, iirc, is the direction John and Holden are going with 3e sidereal charms. It is still a closed charmset, but future books will/might retroactively add to it)</div> </div> </div> </div>There's another possibility that always seemed implied by the text. It doesn't say that Sidereals can't create new Charms, only that the Maidens are the only ones with enough understanding of the entire Loom to create Sidereal Charms that don't cause problems with Fate. That could be taken to mean that Sidereals could create new Charms, only their Charms cause Paradox or localized Fate glitches. I was going to do a write up on that, but then Glories: Maidens came out and stole most of my good ideas as Astrological Charms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520732-forged-by-purpose-alchemicals-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Forged By Purpose: The Alchemicals</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1413451-dead-but-not-gone-ghosts\" target=\"_blank\">Dead But Not Gone: Ghosts</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/228291-ghosts-a-revision-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Ghosts: A Revision</a> (2nd Edition)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/316-masters-of-the-industrial-elements-2e-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Masters of the Industrial Elements</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1157362-from-the-crucible-crafting-as-a-struggle-peach\" target=\"_blank\">\u200bFrom The Crucible: Crafting As A Struggle</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/74-kyeudo","name":"Kyeudo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar74_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1723"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-28T11:00:33-07:00","id":121045,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Hug Ninja</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/120248-sidereal-charms-do-not-work-that-way-and-other-forum-memes?p=120274#post120274\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There tends to be a way certain storytellers run Sidereal NPCs that reinforce a lot of misconceptions about them.<br /> I know at least one person who sincerely believes that virtually every Sidereal their PCs encounter will Avoidance Kata away without provocation, pride secrecy above all else and generally add nothing to the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Important: does he believe the the Sidereals will hug a PC before using Avoidance Kata willy-nilly, like some sort of mysterious sneaky... hugging... ninja... thing?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2144-guancyto","name":"Guancyto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"699"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-28T11:12:34-07:00","id":121052,"title":"","content":"I haven't read 1E Sids in a while, but I do know that 2E incorporates some of these ideas: One of the War charms' flavor text says that it was made by the Maidens right before the Usurpation; another states that the Sids petitioned the Maidens for altenate versions of the Charm to affect various types of being, and that they obliged. <br /> <br /> As for Medicine, the Sid errata mentions that the original Sids were pretty confused by those charms, with the Maidens telling them to &quot;just wait&quot; presumably, but later understood their use...<br /> <br /> As to Breaking Wild Mortals, DotFA kind of touches on this, by having the ability to make Acquaintances do something else before the breaking of the Mask. Possibly this charm had other uses back then, and changing the stars changed it as well. But note that it is required for the &quot;mortal digivolve into dragon&quot; charm! So, it had to have always been there, or maybe Sids couldn't do that in the FA? Or can the Maidens retroactively insert a charm anywhere into a charm tree when they create them? <br /> <br /> Can an Ability have more than one Prayer Strip charm? Can the Maidens create a Charm over Ess 5 if they want? Would all such charms have to have prayer strips?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-28T17:50:53-07:00","id":121327,"title":"","content":"I... like is the wrong word, because this thought kind of annoys me. I have trended by thoughts towards that many Sids have attempted to Create new charms all on their own. Every attempt that had a full and awesome effort into it ended with them inventing a new martial art instead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1252-god_of_awesome","name":"God_of_Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1252_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-30T10:10:35-07:00","id":122438,"title":"","content":"Special thanks to Limited Reagent for reporting actual play experience. <br /> <br /> One reason I am not such a fan of the 1e Sidereals book is that while lots of people raved about its writing and the &quot;surrealism&quot; (another You Keep Using That Word situation) of Sidereal powers, from what I hear not many people played Sidereals. One core purpose of a splatbook is to make you want to play the splat, and <b>Exalted: the Sidereals</b> didn't do that. (The paragraph in the Astrology section about how the system is <i>supposed to be</i> complicated, tedious and not-fun because, y'know, Sidereals operate in a bureaucracy is one of my nominees for Worst Gaming Advice Ever.) <br /> <br /> Reports from people who cut through the blither about how Sidereals are soooo weird and difficult and too cool for you make them sound a lot more fun to play. I hope that 3e takes a more straightforward approach to explaining how they operate and how to play one. <br /> <br /> Dean Shomshak","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1175-dshomshak","name":"DShomshak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"197"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-30T10:32:32-07:00","id":122462,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrInsecure</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/120248-sidereal-charms-do-not-work-that-way-and-other-forum-memes#post120248\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Sidereals Work Best When They Plan Ahead</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Can't believe I'm the first to mention this but but ... really? Are we saying there are Exalted (or other character types) out there who are somehow handicapped by having time to plan? Everyone does better by being prepared. That's more or less the definition of being prepared.<br /> <br /> Sidereals might in theory make the 'preparedness' resource stretch a little longer, but in my experience the astrology rules have been too much rubbish to make that the case. The Sidereal game I played in was not one where we sat back, tented our fingers and said 'everything is going to plan. Rather it was one where we tried to convince everyone else that was happening was to plan while hiding the fact we were pissing ourselves in terror.<br /> <br /> (My favourite destruction of Gem so far came because Sidereal opponents stole Brilliant Beacon's identity and made him invisible to the Celestial Bureaucracy. This totally blocked the political manoeuvring he was engaged with, but didn't stop him from stealing a Warstrider and hurling a Hearthstone into the volcano, causing it to erupt. Afterwards they made sure his identity was very firmly established ... for some reason.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1849,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1849-suddenthunder","user":"SuddenThunder","date":".  Browser issues 04-30-2014, 01:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1849-suddenthunder","name":"SuddenThunder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1849_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-30T10:52:32-07:00","id":122476,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SuddenThunder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/120248-sidereal-charms-do-not-work-that-way-and-other-forum-memes?p=122462#post122462\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can't believe I'm the first to mention this but but ... really? Are we saying there are Exalted (or other character types) out there who are somehow handicapped by having time to plan? Everyone does better by being prepared. That's more or less the definition of being prepared.</div> </div> </div> </div>This has probably been covered elsewhere, but I'm not sure that's actually where the &quot;Sidereals and Planning&quot; connection comes up. It's not that they don't benefit, but that they benefit more than other characters might. I think the idea comes from how some of their Charms are potent, but in a somewhat limited and often strange capacity. They're not the things you will necessarily want to reach for in every situation. Part of the &quot;planning&quot; idea (along with part of the &quot;manipulators&quot; idea) comes in as a result of thinking that Sidereals may want to steer circumstances toward those limited circumstances to get the most out of those Charms. If they're going for particular chokepoints, it can be beneficial to plot out a basic course in advance.<br /> <br /> Note that this comes from observation of one who has not played Sidereals (nor even much Exalted, alas) and who has no idea how well it achieves this in play. Just full-disclosure on how much weight to give that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-30T10:53:36-07:00","id":122477,"title":"","content":"Hmmm, Sidereal does have access to Yu-Shan's gigantic web of information and influence so any Sid that want to become a manipulator will have an easier time than other splat. And charm like Wise Choice or Prior Warning make Sidereal's plan having the best chance of success among the Exalted<br /> <br /> But I assume that the people who use &quot;<b>Sidereals Work Best When They Plan Ahead&quot; </b>often say them in a very....fluffy and 'Cause-the-Book-Say-So kind of way with no mention of why or how can they accomplish those &quot;Plans Within Plans&quot; stuff In-Character. Not to mention most people can't really resist the temptation for splat-stereotype.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-30T11:37:57-07:00","id":122532,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SuddenThunder</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <i>Everyone does better by being prepared. That's more or less the definition of being prepared. </i></div> </div> </div> </div>It's pretty easy to imagine characters who work better and achieve more when they're behaving spontaneously and improvising, though. Planning ahead (which er, isn't *exactly* a synonym for being prepared) just leads some folks to choke or abstract themselves from the actual situation at hand and fail.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DShomshak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/120248-sidereal-charms-do-not-work-that-way-and-other-forum-memes?p=122438#post122438\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One reason I am not such a fan of the 1e Sidereals book is that while lots of people raved about its writing and the &quot;surrealism&quot; (another You Keep Using That Word situation) of Sidereal powers, from what I hear not many people played Sidereals. One core purpose of a splatbook is to make you want to play the splat, and <b>Exalted: the Sidereals</b> didn't do that. (The paragraph in the Astrology section about how the system is <i>supposed to be</i> complicated, tedious and not-fun because, y'know, Sidereals operate in a bureaucracy is one of my nominees for Worst Gaming Advice Ever.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the 1e Exalted did pretty well, even if it has a lot of imperfections with hindsight. Sidereals are never going to be top of the splat, and it's seems like the slightly soiled copypasta Manual of Exalted Power and internet echo chamber probably have at least as much to do with Sidereals not being more popular.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-30T12:30:30-07:00","id":122573,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/120248-sidereal-charms-do-not-work-that-way-and-other-forum-memes?p=122532#post122532\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's pretty easy to imagine characters who work better and achieve more when they're behaving spontaneously and improvising, though. Planning ahead (which er, isn't *exactly* a synonym for being prepared) just leads some folks to choke or abstract themselves from the actual situation at hand and fail.</div> </div> </div> </div>It would be interesting if Lunar Charms evoked this for the Lunar Exalted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-30T15:10:29-07:00","id":122687,"title":"","content":"Honestly, I'd like to see things changed from &quot;Sidereals plan&quot; to &quot;Sidereals hide the rulebook, won't tell you what game is being played, and cheat outrageously the entire time.&quot; <br /> Besides, didn't someone famously say that no plan survives contact with the Gamemaster? <br /> I'd like to see more Charms like Murder Moving Finger Dance and that one Drive charm that lets you rummage around in your trunk and pull out whatever you need, and less like the Craft one where you where each activation might move an object the length of a gnat's ass towards where you need it, provided you've been very good, the weather is only partly cloudly, and it feels like working. And Maidens piss on you if you've been moving the wrong object with it all these months.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Have you ever read a Coik post before, man? lol<br /> -Holden<br /> <br />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/338-coik","name":"Coik","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar338_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"611"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-30T18:33:52-07:00","id":122828,"title":"","content":"Pretty much what Coik said, yeah.<br /> <br /> Sometimes I think the reason people go so heavily on the &quot;Sidereals work best when they plan ahead&quot; meme is so that they have an excuse to say &quot;and so it's okay that they're sub-par when surprised, blindsided, ambushed or otherwise in situations PCs tend to find themselves in.&quot; (Seriously, when was the last campaign anyone had when the GM didn't spring surprises on them?) As a Sidereal player I don't actually find that okay, and to be honest, I wouldn't mind if &quot;planning ahead&quot; got abstracted into something I can pull out on the fly OOCly, instead of forcing me to try to read the GM's mind at all times. (I'm also pretty sure that GMs in general would appreciate Sidereal players not converting every other session into a Shadowrun-level planning session. This has happened more than once to my Sidereal group.) I also wouldn't mind if it stopped being an excuse not to bring their toolkits up to Celestial standards.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/39-ysadrel","name":"ysadrel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-01T01:02:07-07:00","id":123012,"title":"","content":"Cheating itself as a theme reminds me of the 2e Ebon Dragon, and what a turnoff that character was. &quot;I want to win. Even, or especially, if it means making everything suck, and making every conflict uncool&quot;, and the players and fans that character appealed to.<br /> <br /> As much as they are about being subject to different rules, Sidereals would be more satisfying if they were sold on being capable rather than succeeding on making others worse by lying to them and hiding information and hypocritically breaking rules they appear to agree to. The characters have to appeal to people beyond certain kinds of dorky, misanthropic, smirking teens who want to play a justified yet amoral antihero. Or leaving this aside, how much can the agents of order really be about cheating and breaking the rules of the system, without this feeling hypocritical and self defeating?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-01T01:08:31-07:00","id":123015,"title":"","content":"I've noticed that on the internet, &quot;meme&quot; apparently means &quot;idea I dislike&quot;.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2160-elemental","name":"Elemental","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2160_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"412"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-01T03:40:53-07:00","id":123041,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/120248-sidereal-charms-do-not-work-that-way-and-other-forum-memes?p=122532#post122532\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's pretty easy to imagine characters who work better and achieve more when they're behaving spontaneously and improvising, though. Planning ahead (which er, isn't *exactly* a synonym for being prepared) just leads some folks to choke or abstract themselves from the actual situation at hand and fail.<br /> <br /> I think the 1e Exalted did pretty well, even if it has a lot of imperfections with hindsight. Sidereals are never going to be top of the splat, and it's seems like the slightly soiled copypasta Manual of Exalted Power and internet echo chamber probably have at least as much to do with Sidereals not being more popular.</div> </div> </div> </div>A large part of why Sidereals are unpopular in my games is that no other splat is quite as hostile to the ST as Sidereals are. It's fine if all the characters are sidereals, but if the last player picks sidereal it means the ST suddenly has to deal with global information networks, powers of prophecy and ancient overpowered NPC's she could just have ignored otherwise. This leads to ST's not being exactly enthusiastic about selling people on Sidereals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/292-zironic","name":"Zironic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar292_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"654"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-01T09:25:22-07:00","id":123214,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elemental</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/120248-sidereal-charms-do-not-work-that-way-and-other-forum-memes?p=123015#post123015\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've noticed that on the internet, &quot;meme&quot; apparently means &quot;idea I dislike&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>And/or &quot;image macro.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-01T09:35:12-07:00","id":123224,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elemental</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/120248-sidereal-charms-do-not-work-that-way-and-other-forum-memes?p=123015#post123015\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've noticed that on the internet, &quot;meme&quot; apparently means &quot;idea I dislike&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=xXK9ShllebQ\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=xXK9ShllebQ\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=xXK9ShllebQ\" target=\"_blank\"> http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=xXK9ShllebQ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=dQw4w9WgXcQ\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\